Subject: Cantor Identity Accounting Journal and Host Protocol P1 Solution

& [ImplementedSolution]
  + AccountingJournal is a complete append-only map of ledger generations connected by semantically replayed events
  + AccountingHostRequest turns inference intentions into strict inspect project resolve read or patch operations
  + AccountingHostResponse binds the exact request journal head typed result and canonical response digest
  + encode and decode operations create a bounded canonical persistence seam without ambient IO

& [NextBoundary]
  + a separately authorized physical storage adapter may atomically persist canonical journal bytes
  + inference prompt and tool adapters may transport strict requests and responses without changing core semantics
  + entity admission removal multi-basket decomposition Judgment and effects remain separate governed successors
